      "body": "## Issue\n\nFixes #33714 — **unified_cache 长 prompt 备份缺失（chunked long-prompt backup missing in unified_cache）**\n\nFor any request whose cold prefill extend exceeds `chunked_prefill_size`, HiCache\nwrite-through was completely skipped. After a server restart, every cold long\nprompt had to pay the full prefill cost again.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nChunked prefill flows through multiple intermediate `checkpoint_kv_cache`\ncalls before the final `release_kv_cache`. Each call passes\n`inserted_len = req.kv.cache_inserted_len`, and `UnifiedTreeCore` skips the\nhit-count bump for any node whose `node_end <= inserted_len`:\n\n| Phase | inserted_len | Retained prefix nodes | Hit count bump |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Chunk 1 checkpoint | 0 | — (all new) | ✓ hit_count += 1 |\n| Chunk 2 checkpoint | chunk_size | chunk 1 nodes | ✗ skipped |\n| Chunk 3 checkpoint | 2× chunk_size | chunk 1 + chunk 2 | ✗ skipped |\n| **Final release insert** | total_len | **all prior nodes** | **✗ skipped** |\n\nResult: every node on the retained prefix ends with `hit_count = 1`. With\n`hicache-write-policy write_through_selective` (threshold = 2), the\nwrite-through backup **never fires** on a cold chunked request.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd `InsertParams.force_bump_hit_count: bool = False`. When set, the tree\nwalk ignores the `inserted_len` gate and bumps hit counts on every node it\npasses — replaying the root-walk effects that a chunked request's intermediate\ncheckpoints deliberately deferred.\n\n`UnifiedRadixCache.checkpoint_into_tree` sets `force_bump_hit_count=True`\n**only** when:\n\n- `is_finished = True` (the final insert, not an intermediate checkpoint), **and**\n- `req.kv.cache_inserted_len > 0` (there was at least one prior intermediate checkpoint,\n  i.e. the request was chunked).\n\nThis gives the retained prefix exactly **one extra hit-count bump at request\nfinish**, bringing every node from `hit_count=1` to `hit_count=2` — just at\nthe `write_through_selective` threshold of 2 so HiCache write-through fires.\n\nNon-chunked requests are unaffected (`cache_inserted_len = 0` at finish →\n`force_bump_hit_count = False`). The split-leaf insert at the prompt boundary\nalso explicitly disables it to avoid a double-bump on the structural re-insert.\n\n## Design Notes\n\n- Mirrors Rust-side fix b7e2cd903a which introduced the same \"bump only on\n  non-chunked continuation\" semantic on the Rust UnifiedTreeCore.\n- Acknowledges PR #36353 (zumi87, open): this approach is complementary —\n  it reuses the existing hit-count->write-through trigger instead of adding a\n  new backup path, keeping the change minimal and fully backward-compatible.\n- Mamba checkpoint boundary edge case (PR #30850) remains open; it requires\n  `effective_cache_len > 0` to enter the insert path at all.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Code compiles clean (`py_compile` on all three touched files).\n- Backward-compatible: `force_bump_hit_count` defaults to `False`.\n- Simulated scenarios (table above) confirm every chunked-request node crosses\n  the `write_through_selective` threshold exactly at request finish.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38633112083](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38633112083)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38633111795](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38633111795)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38633111669](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38633111669)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
